  "result": "Perfect! All 138 tests pass! Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**Changes to `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **Added `lineVAT(line)` function:**\n   - Calculates VAT on the taxable amount: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100`\n   - VAT is rounded per line using `roundCents()`\n   - Returns result object with VAT amount\n\n2. **Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)` return structure:**\n   - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - Calculates VAT for each line and sums them\n   - Formula: `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n   - All amounts clamped to 0 minimum (no negative amounts)\n\n**Changes to `src/render.js`:**\n- Shows `VAT: \u20acX.XX` line when VAT > 0, positioned just above the total\n- When discounts are present, shows: Subtotal \u2192 Discount \u2192 VAT \u2192 Total\n- When no discounts but VAT present: shows VAT \u2192 Total\n- When neither: shows Total only\n\n**Key VAT behavior:**\n- VAT is calculated per line on the amount after discount (taxable amount)\n- Different lines can have different VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n- Invoice VAT is the sum of all rounded line VATs\n- VAT is completely separate from discount calculations\n- Tier discounts reduce the taxable amount for VAT purposes\n\n**Added 16 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- VAT calculation with and without discounts\n- Different VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0% exempt)\n- Multiple lines with mixed VAT rates\n- VAT totals and rendering\n- Edge cases (100% discount, VAT exempt items)\n\nAll 138 tests pass! \u2713",
